  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "For any complex number \\(w=a+bi,\\) \\(|w|\\) is defined to be the real number \\(\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}.\\) If \\(w=\\cos40^\\circ+i\\sin40^\\circ,\\) then \\[ |w+2w^2+3w^3+\\cdots+9w^9|^{-1} \\] equals",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\frac19\\sin40^\\circ\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\frac29\\sin20^\\circ\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\frac19\\cos40^\\circ\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\frac1{18}\\cos20^\\circ\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "none of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1984-p30.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(S=\\sum_{k=1}^9kw^k.\\) Since \\(w^9=1\\) and \\(w^{10}=w,\\) \\[ \\begin{aligned} (1-w)S &=(w+w^2+\\cdots+w^9)\\\\ &\\quad-9w^{10}\\\\ &=-9w. \\end{aligned} \\] Therefore \\(|S|=\\frac{9}{|1-w|},\\) because \\(|w|=1.\\) Thus \\[ |S|^{-1}=\\frac{|1-w|}{9} =\\frac{2}{9}\\sin20^\\circ. \\] Therefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Let \\(S=w+2w^2+\\cdots+9w^9\\) and subtract \\(wS\\) from \\(S\\)",
        "Use \\(w^9=1\\) and \\(|1-e^{i\\theta}|=2\\sin(\\frac{\\theta}{2})\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
